    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0102" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg52"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Le Ghait to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Belgium,</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-23"><hi rendition="#italic">December 23,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: The Belgian Government
                    has received, as the United States Government doubtless has also, a letter from
                    the London International Statistical Institute, advocating a meeting of an
                    international commission for the unification of the systems of admeasuring
                    seagoing vessels that are now in force in the different countries.</p>
                <p>My Government would be glad to be acquainted with the views of the United States
                    Government in relation to this proposition. So far as it is concerned, it would
                    be glad to see this measure carried out, as its utility appears incontestable,
                    and it is prepared to cooperate in any efforts that may be made to this end.</p>
                <p>I beg, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Le Ghait</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
